    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0344" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg274"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Señor Don Alberto Blest Gana</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 11, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:. I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of a despatch<anchor n="†" xml:id="d167-f1"/> which has been addressed by
                    the department to the United States minister at Madrid on the subject of the
                    propositions for a peace conference contained in the circular despatch which
                    issued from this department on the 20th of last December.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to assure you of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alberto Blest Gana,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d167-f1" n="†" xml:id="d167-f1-content">
                <p>For enclosure see instruction to United States minister to Spain, No. 59.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
